{"seq":1,"slug":"shaping-chinese-culture","title":"Shaping Chinese Culture","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/influence-and-legacy/shaping-chinese-culture","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"laozhuang-and-daoism","title":"老庄与道家道教","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/influence-and-legacy/shaping-chinese-culture/laozhuang-and-daoism","wordCount":2134,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"art-and-literature","title":"文学与艺术","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/influence-and-legacy/shaping-chinese-culture/art-and-literature","wordCount":2013,"readingTime":9}],"introHtml":"<p>本章呈现庄子对中国文化的塑造。庄子与老子并称&quot;老庄&quot;,共同构成道家思想的核心，与儒家互补、深刻地影响了道教（唐代被尊为&quot;南华真人&quot;），共同塑造了中国人的精神世界。他那汪洋恣肆的想象、追求自由的精神、崇尚自然的趣味，更开创了中国浪漫主义文学（影响李白等）与写意艺术的源头，深刻地塑造了中国艺术的审美精神。本章揭示庄子对中国文化的深远塑造。</p>\n"}